1.2-.806-1.2-1.8s.537-1.8 1.2-1.8c.663 0 1.2.806 1.2 1.8s-.537 1.8-1.2 1.8Z\" fill=\"#fff\"></path><path d=\"M11.199 10.795h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM12.56 10.795h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM13.92 10.795h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM11.199 9.364h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM12.56 9.364h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM13.92 9.364h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM15.28 9.364H14.2v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM11.199 7.982h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM12.56 7.982h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM13.92 7.982h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM15.28 7.982H14.2v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM12.56 6.545h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM13.92 6.545h-1.08v1.16h1.08v-1.16ZM15.28 6.545H14.2v1.16h1.08v-1.16Z\" fill=\"#1976D2\"></path></svg><!--]--><!--]--></div><!--]--> <div class=\"content-container svelte-17nnmqu\"><!--[-1--><!---->Outlook desktop<!----><!--]--></div> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----></button><!----><!----></li> <li class=\"svelte-5h8gi0\"><!----><button data-variant=\"secondary\" data-size=\"m\" class=\"Btn  svelte-17nnmqu f-label-3\" type=\"button\" aria-disabled=\"true\" data-loading=\"false\"><!--[0--><div class=\"right-container svelte-17nnmqu\"><!--[1--><!--[--><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M.501 4.395h3.433l1.998 5.113 2.025-5.113H11.3L6.267 16.5H2.903l1.378-3.208L.5 4.395Zm14.69 4.086h-3.744L14.77.5h3.73L15.19 8.48Zm-2.763.764a2.08 2.08 0 1 1 0 4.158 2.08 2.08 0 0 1 0-4.158Z\" fill=\"#5F01D1\"></path></svg><!--]--><!--]--></div><!--]--> <div class=\"content-container svelte-17nnmqu\"><!--[-1--><!---->Yahoo<!----><!--]--></div> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----></button><!----><!----></li></ul><!----></div><!----></div><!----><!----></div> <button class=\"ModalCloseButton svelte-t3wwh4\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Close dialog\" data-trap-boundary=\"last\" data-button-style=\"flat\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 15 15\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" class=\"CrossIcon\" aria-label=\"Cross icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Close icon</title><path d=\"M11.782 4.032a.575.575 0 1 0-.813-.814L7.5 6.687 4.032 3.218a.575.575 0 0 0-.814.814L6.687 7.5l-3.469 3.468a.575.575 0 0 0 .814.814L7.5 8.313l3.469 3.469a.575.575 0 0 0 .813-.814L8.313 7.5l3.469-3.468Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg><!----><span class=\"u-visually-hidden\">Close</span></button><!----><!----></dialog><!----></div><!----> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class=\"EventModules svelte-r64kdn\"><!--[--><!--[0--><!--[9--><div class=\"EventModuleRichText svelte-6ayzyh\"><!--[0--><h2 class=\"title f-heading-4 svelte-6ayzyh\">Description</h2><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <div class=\"RichContent f-body-3 svelte-jgfn07\"><!--[0--><!----><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><strong>The Roger Ely Experience - A Cabaret</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><strong>Thursday 12 November 2026</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><strong>20.00 </strong></span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><strong>Tickets £12.50/£10 concessions </strong></span><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#3c2e4e;--custom-color-dark:#d8caea\"><strong>*see note</strong></span><strong><br /></strong></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><strong>An evening celebrating the life and legacy of Roger Ely </strong>featuring short turns and films by a wide range of artists, musicians and film makers connected to Roger.  Performers: <strong>Liz Aggiss, </strong></span><strong>Steve Beresford, The Neo Naturists, Richard Strange, Dorothy Max Prior, Phil Minton, Dave Stephens </strong>and<strong> Neil Butler </strong>+ short films.</p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Roger Ely (1952-2015) was an extraordinary and influential artist, publisher, archivist, curator, and collector. This event marks the British Library’s acquisition of Roger’s extensive and unique archive, enabling generations to come to discover a significant, rare and unrivalled history of the alternative and counterculture of the late twentieth century.  </span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">From Leeds Arts School in the 1960s, to the Brighton Contemporary Festival of Arts in the 1970s, to the Final Academy in the 1980s, to the Zap Club in the 1990s, Roger Ely was at the centre of the underground scene that influenced the art, music, film, literature, cabaret and performance that went on to change the world.  </span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">His collaborators, connections and collections are breathtaking - William Burroughs, Brion Gysin, Ian Hinchliffe, Genesis P-Orridge, John Giorno, Kathy Acker, John Maybury, Cosey Fanni Tutti, Lydia Lunch, Marc Almond, Kenneth Williams, Anne Bean. Paul Burwell, Derek Jarman and countless other luminaries and characters all feature in some way in his life and in his archive.</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><strong>The Water Rats </strong>cabaret follows a discussion at the nearby <strong>British Library</strong> from 6pm to 7.30, looking at Roger’s archive and the cultural landscapes it shines a light on with <strong>Steve Cleary, Dave Stephens, Neil Butler, Lois Keidan, Anne Bean, Barry Miles </strong>and<strong> Rob La Frenais</strong>.  </span><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#1d768c;--custom-color-dark:#86d9ef\">GET YOUR British Library </span><a rel=\"nofollow\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://events.bl.uk/events/the-roger-ely-experience\"><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#1d768c;--custom-color-dark:#86d9ef\"><strong>TICKETS HERE</strong></span></a></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#5c4677;--custom-color-dark:#ddc7f8\"><strong>*And NOTE:</strong></span><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#1d768c;--custom-color-dark:#86d9ef\"><strong> </strong></span><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Tickets to <strong>British Library</strong> w</span>ill <strong>also enable entry</strong> to the Cabaret at the <strong>Water Rats,</strong> later the same evening so <span style=\"--custom-color-light:#5c4677;--custom-color-dark:#ddc7f8\"><strong>if you're booking a British Library Ticket there is no need to book a separate Water Rats Ticket on this site.</strong></span></p><!----><!--]--></div><!----></div><!--]--><!--]--><!--[0--><!--[10--><dialog class=\"ModalShell svelte-14yzxqa\" aria-label=\"Gallery image viewer\" data-transition-intent=\"none\"><div class=\"CarouselModal svelte-1subrpe\" data-surface=\"background\" data-desktop-height=\"fixed\"><button class=\"ModalCloseButton svelte-t3wwh4\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Close dialog\" data-trap-boundary=\"first\" data-button-style=\"round\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 15 15\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" class=\"CrossIcon\" aria-label=\"Cross icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Close icon</title><path d=\"M11.782 4.032a.575.575 0 1 0-.813-.814L7.5 6.687 4.032 3.218a.575.575 0 0 0-.814.814L6.687 7.5l-3.469 3.468a.575.575 0 0 0 .814.814L7.5 8.313l3.469 3.469a.575.575 0 0 0 .813-.814L8.313 7.5l3.469-3.468Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg><!----><span class=\"u-visually-hidden\">Close</span></button><!----> <div class=\"content svelte-1subrpe\"><!--[-1--><!--]--><!----></div> <!--[0--><footer class=\"ModalFooter svelte-1y1b7pd\" data-surface=\"background\"><!--[0--><div class=\"progress-bar svelte-1subrpe\"><div class=\"progress-bar-fill svelte-1subrpe\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div></div> <span class=\"progress-text svelte-1subrpe\">0 / 27</span><!--]--> <button type=\"button\" class=\"navigation-button svelte-1subrpe\" data-su