.65Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></g></svg><!----></footer><!--]--> <button class=\"ModalCloseButton svelte-t3wwh4\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Close dialog\" data-trap-boundary=\"last\" data-button-style=\"round\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 15 15\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" class=\"CrossIcon\" aria-label=\"Cross icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Close icon</title><path d=\"M11.782 4.032a.575.575 0 1 0-.813-.814L7.5 6.687 4.032 3.218a.575.575 0 0 0-.814.814L6.687 7.5l-3.469 3.468a.575.575 0 0 0 .814.814L7.5 8.313l3.469 3.469a.575.575 0 0 0 .813-.814L8.313 7.5l3.469-3.468Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg><!----><span class=\"u-visually-hidden\">Close</span></button><!----></div></dialog><!--]--></div><!----><!----><!----> <!----><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"The Roger Ely Experience\",\"url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/the-roger-ely-experience\",\"startDate\":\"2026-11-12T20:00:00+0000\",\"endDate\":\"2026-11-12T22:30:00+0000\",\"location\":{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"The Water Rats\",\"address\":{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"328 Gray's Inn Rd, London WC1X 8BZ, UK\",\"postalCode\":\"WC1X 8BZ\",\"addressRegion\":\"England\",\"addressCountry\":\"GB\"}},\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"description\":\"artists celebrate the life and art of Roger Ely in a cabaret format at the Water Rats – it follows an event at the British Library on Roger's archive and legacy\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/933d4a43-6328-49ab-a075-16936733a7e8.png@seo-500.jpg\",\"offers\":[{\"@type\":\"AggregateOffer\",\"offerCount\":2,\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"availabilityStarts\":\"2026-07-27T12:51:41.127Z\",\"availability\":\"InStock\",\"availabilityEnds\":\"2026-11-12T22:30:00.800Z\"},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/the-roger-ely-experience/tickets\",\"name\":\"General Admission\",\"price\":12.5,\"availability\":\"InStock\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\"},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/the-roger-ely-experience/tickets\",\"name\":\"concession\",\"price\":10,\"availability\":\"InStock\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\"}],\"performers\":[{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Liz Aggiss\",\"description\":\"Liz Aggiss is an un-disciplined artist with an un-disciplined body of work. This does not mean she is undisciplined. Au contraire. She is exceptionally disciplined. Dodging categorisation and being classified as unclassifiable, has been a full time job. She has been described as: maverick, challenging, anarchic, indomitable, dangerous, uncompromising, subversive, fearless, funny, powerfully disturbing yet vulnerable.\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/a0052ab0-7a96-4e53-aaf9-ca435a778bb5.png@seo-500.jpg\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Steve Beresford\",\"description\":\"Steve Beresford has played piano with improvisers like Derek Bailey and also trumpet with the notorious Portsmouth Sinfonia. He has worked with the Slits, Han Bennink, Christine Tobin, Ivor Cutler, Prince Far-I, Vic Reeves, Alan Hacker, Ray Davies, Ilan Volkov, Najma Akhtar, Evan Parker, Adrian Sherwood, The Flying Lizards, Stewart Lee, Otomo Yoshihide and John Zorn. Free improvisation is central, generally involving piano and/or electronics. He also writes songs, TV and film music, directs ensembles and has been known to sing and write.\\n\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/3a77adf1-b982-4c64-94e2-104f7ab4eaab.jpg@seo-500.jpg\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Neil Butler\",\"description\":\"Neil Butler first performed in public aged seventeen and since then worked as an artist, creative producer and cultural strategist. Co-founder with Roger of Brighton’s Contemporary Arts Festival, he launched the Zap Club and large-scale multi-art form productions in London, Streetbiz and UZ Arts in Glasgow and Sura Medura in Sri Lanka. Along the way there’s been festivals across Scotland and the UK and projects that have spanned Europe and the World.\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/930ba0ad-89d0-42a8-8efc-f873e4706599.jpg@seo-500.jpg\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Phil Minton\",\"description\":\"Phil Minton played trumpet and sang with the Mike Westbrook Band in the early 1960s and then in bands across Europe before rejoining Westbrook until the mid 1980s. He has been an improvising singer in groups and orchestras and composers have written pieces that especially employ his extended vocal techniques and improvisations. He has a quartet with Veryan Weston, Roger Turner and John Butcher and ongoing duos with all the above. He also sings with Audrey Chen, Carl Ludwig Hübsch, Guylaine Cosseron, Hugh Medcalfe and Szilard Mezei.\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/5a3f4684-ce12-486e-a927-201a05d64828.jpg@seo-500.jpg\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"The Neo Naturists \",\"description\":\"The Neo Naturists are a performance art group founded by Christine Binnie, Jennifer Binnie and Wilma Johnson. The group emerged from a subculture – connected with but not limited to the New Romantic club scene. The most intense period of activity was during the early to mid 1980s with regular performances in nightclubs and galleries. In 2016 they had a ‘Live’ retrospective at Studio Voltaire with an evening of live art at the ICA.\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/795c9ebd-2b34-4c9a-b471-1a272191e3e0.png@seo-500.jpg\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Dorothy Max Prior\",\"description\":\"Dorothy Max Prior has worked in performance, spoken word and sound installation. She has published two bestselling volumes of her life and times:  69 Exhibition Road and Sex is No Emergency. She is editor of Total Theatre Magazine and writes for and edits other arts publications. She has a fortnightly show on Slack City Radio: Granny (Max) Takes a Trip. In other lives, Max was a punk muse, post-punk drummer (with Rema Rema and Psychic TV, amongst others) and exotic dancer. Somewhere along the way, she has taught ballroom dancing and toured the world as a cabaret artist, street theatre performer, choreographer, and director.\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/cff5d178-2162-4006-b983-f53418be5272.png@seo-500.jpg\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Dave Stephens\",\"description\":\"Dave Stephens first came to public attention as a performance artist. After leaving Leeds Polytechnic where he studied alongside Roger in the Fine Art department under Jeff Nuttal, Roland Miller and John Darling he joined John Bull Puncture Repair Kit and toured Britain and Europe. He teamed up with Ian Hinchliffe, Roger and others in the Matchbox Purveyors for visual and verbal tours through the absurdist imagination. Nowadays, his practise often moves between disciplines and some of his recent work combines elements of all of them. \\n\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/75ca2a3e-aed3-4d7b-8c51-9b035258de0d.png@seo-500.jpg\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Richard Strange\",\"description\":\"Since the Doctors of Madness was first unleashed on an uncomprehending public in 1975, Strange has been a Zelig-like figure whose presence has been felt in every corner of London’s cultural life. He founded the hugely influential mixed-media Cabaret Futura in 1980, and has subsequently worked as a musician, writer and actor on stage and screen. He’s worked with Marianne Faithfull, Gavin Bryars, Jarvis Cocker, Hal Wilner and numerous other luminaries. Movie appearances include Batman, Mona Lisa, and Gangs of New York and he recently filmed the last episode of Harry Potter.\",\"image\":\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/b3d171b8-502b-4a38-8025-8cd90398f19e.jpg@seo-500.jpg\"}]}</script><!----> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!----><!--]--><!--]-->