16.5H2.903l1.378-3.208L.5 4.395Zm14.69 4.086h-3.744L14.77.5h3.73L15.19 8.48Zm-2.763.764a2.08 2.08 0 1 1 0 4.158 2.08 2.08 0 0 1 0-4.158Z\" fill=\"#5F01D1\"></path></svg><!--]--><!--]--></div><!--]--> <div class=\"content-container svelte-17nnmqu\"><!--[-1--><!---->Yahoo<!----><!--]--></div> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----></button><!----><!----></li></ul><!----></div><!----></div><!----><!----></div> <button class=\"ModalCloseButton svelte-t3wwh4\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Close dialog\" data-trap-boundary=\"last\" data-button-style=\"flat\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 15 15\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" class=\"CrossIcon\" aria-label=\"Cross icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Close icon</title><path d=\"M11.782 4.032a.575.575 0 1 0-.813-.814L7.5 6.687 4.032 3.218a.575.575 0 0 0-.814.814L6.687 7.5l-3.469 3.468a.575.575 0 0 0 .814.814L7.5 8.313l3.469 3.469a.575.575 0 0 0 .813-.814L8.313 7.5l3.469-3.468Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg><!----><span class=\"u-visually-hidden\">Close</span></button><!----><!----></dialog><!----></div><!----> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class=\"EventModules svelte-r64kdn\"><!--[--><!--[0--><!--[9--><div class=\"EventModuleRichText svelte-6ayzyh\"><!--[0--><h2 class=\"title f-heading-4 svelte-6ayzyh\">Description</h2><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <div class=\"RichContent f-body-3 svelte-jgfn07\"><!--[0--><!----><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">The landmark queer film of the silent era, <em>Mikaël</em> (with the more blatant alternative title of <em>Chained: The Story of the Third Sex</em>) is screening at the Finch Community Cinema as the third installment of our Silent Films are Gay! Series.</span><br /><br /><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Before directing such monumental fixtures of cinema as <em>The Passion of Joan of Arc, Vampyr</em>, and <em>Days of Wrath</em>, Carl Theodor Dreyer experimented with his first signature close shots in Mikaël, adapted from the novel by gay writer Herman Bang. Master artist Claude Zoret (Benjamin Christensen, filmmaker of <em>Häxan</em>) finds his muse and lover, the young, handsome Mikaël (Walter Slezak) slipping away, just as the world, and his place in it does. <em>Mikaël</em> is a sweeping, emotive, visually lush portrait of queer love and heartbreak, and the artistic acceptance of mortality. </span><br /><br /><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Harangued by critics of its day for its not-so subliminal queer themes, Mikaël has become a fixture of queer cinema history, and an undeniable must to be included in our Silent Films are Gay Season.</span><br /><br /><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">The film will be live accompanied by Cyrus Gabrysch, who has worked with the BFI, London Film Festival, and English National Ballet, and will include a special introduction from theatre director and playwright Alex Hurst. </span><br /><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><br />Tickets are £7, with 15% of all sales donated to MAP (Medical Aid for Palestinians).<br />Doors 6:30pm, Film starts 7pm.</span></p><!----><!--]--></div><!----></div><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></div><!--]--> <div class=\"HumanitixBannerLarge svelte-17kav4o\"><div class=\"logos svelte-17kav4o\"><span class=\"powered-by f-label-1 svelte-17kav4o\">Powered by</span> <svg class=\"HumanitixLogoSvg svelte-pxa59x\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 139 34\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Humanitix logo</title><g><!--[-1--><!--]--><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M12.37 23.84c-1.06 0-1.62-.57-1.62-1.63v-2.73a.66.66 0 0 0-.72-.72H6.35a.66.66 0 0 0-.72.72v2.73c0 1.06-.56 1.63-1.62 1.63H1.62C.56 23.84 0 23.27 0 22.2v-10.2c0-1.06.56-1.62 1.62-1.62h2.4c1.05 0 1.61.56 1.61 1.62v1.84a.66.66 