h)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"medium\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-medium)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"low\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-low)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"disabled\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-disabled)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"primary\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-primary)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"success\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-success)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"error\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-error)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"warning\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-warning)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"info\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-info)}\\n        }\\n    \",ticketButtonText:\"Get tickets\"},settings:{afterCheckoutRedirect:void 0,allowTicketAndMerchSwaps:false,allowUserEdit:true,codesViaLinkOnly:false,disableHumanitixGTM:false,hideAddToCalendar:false,hideArtistPreviews:false,removeImpactCommunication:false,requireEmailConfirmation:false,sendTickets:true,noTicketsMessagingOption:\"none\",showTicketsLeft:false,minimumTicketsPerOrder:void 0,maximumTicketsPerOrder:void 0,seatingMapEditable:false,enableV3SeatMaps:false,waitlistEnabled:false,salesStopped:false,hideConfetti:false,mobileRequired:true},eventModules:[{component:\"richtext\",props:{title:\"Description\",content:\"\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\\\">The landmark queer film of the silent era, \\u003Cem>Mikaël\\u003C/em> (with the more blatant alternative title of \\u003Cem>Chained: The Story of the Third Sex\\u003C/em>) is screening at the Finch Community Cinema as the third installment of our Silent Films are Gay! Series.\\u003C/span>\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\\\">Before directing such monumental fixtures of cinema as \\u003Cem>The Passion of Joan of Arc, Vampyr\\u003C/em>, and \\u003Cem>Days of Wrath\\u003C/em>, Carl Theodor Dreyer experimented with his first signature close shots in Mikaël, adapted from the novel by gay writer Herman Bang. Master artist Claude Zoret (Benjamin Christensen, filmmaker of \\u003Cem>Häxan\\u003C/em>) finds his muse and lover, the young, handsome Mikaël (Walter Slezak) slipping away, just as the world, and his place in it does. \\u003Cem>Mikaël\\u003C/em> is a sweeping, emotive, visually lush portrait of queer love and heartbreak, and the artistic acceptance of mortality. \\u003C/span>\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\\\">Harangued by critics of its day for its not-so subliminal queer themes, Mikaël has become a fixture of queer cinema history, and an undeniable must to be included in our Silent Films are Gay Season.\\u003C/span>\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\\\">The film will be live accompanied by Cyrus Gabrysch, who has worked with the BFI, London Film Festival, and English National Ballet, and will include a special introduction from theatre director and playwright Alex Hurst. \\u003C/span>\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#202020;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\\\">\\u003Cbr />Tickets are £7, with 15% of all sales donated to MAP (Medical Aid for Palestinians).\\u003Cbr />Doors 6:30pm, Film starts 7pm.\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\"}}],artists:[],seo:{jsonSchema:{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",name:\"Films are Gay! presents: Mikaël (1924, dir. Carl Theodor Dreyer) with live score!\",url:\"https://events.humanitix.com/films-are-gay-presents-mikael-1924-dir-carl-theodor-dreyer-with-live-score\",startDate:\"2026-10-03T18:30:00+0100\",endDate:\"2026-10-03T21:00:00+0100\",location:{\"@type\":\"Place\",name:\"Finch Cafe/Restaurant\",address:{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",streetAddress:\"12 Sidworth St, London E8 3SD, UK\",postalCode:\"E8 3SD\",addressRegion:\"England\",addressCountry:\"GB\"}},eventStatus:\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",eventAttendanceMode:\"https://schema.org/OfflineEvent