-colorv3-current-border:var(--colorv3-sunken-border);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tbackground:var(--colorv3-sunken-base);color:var(--colorv3-current-text-high);\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t[data-surface*=\\\"sunken\\\"][data-surface*=\\\"interactive\\\"]:hover{background:var(--colorv3-sunken-hover)}\\n\\t\\t\\t[data-surface*=\\\"sunken\\\"][data-surface*=\\\"interactive\\\"]:active{background:var(--colorv3-sunken-active)}\\n\\t\\n\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"high\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-high)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"medium\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-medium)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"low\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-low)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"disabled\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-disabled)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"primary\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-primary)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"success\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-success)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"error\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-error)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"warning\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-warning)}\\n\\t[data-text=\\\"info\\\"]{color:var(--colorv3-current-text-info)}\\n        }\\n    \",ticketButtonText:\"Get tickets\"},settings:{afterCheckoutRedirect:void 0,allowTicketAndMerchSwaps:false,allowUserEdit:true,codesViaLinkOnly:false,disableHumanitixGTM:false,hideAddToCalendar:false,hideArtistPreviews:false,removeImpactCommunication:false,requireEmailConfirmation:false,sendTickets:true,noTicketsMessagingOption:\"none\",showTicketsLeft:false,minimumTicketsPerOrder:void 0,maximumTicketsPerOrder:void 0,seatingMapEditable:false,enableV3SeatMaps:false,waitlistEnabled:false,salesStopped:false,hideConfetti:false,mobileRequired:true},eventModules:[{component:\"richtext\",props:{title:\"Description\",content:\"\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">\\u003Cstrong>When the storm comes, where is the way out?\\u003C/strong>\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">Inspired by documented cases of domestic violence, \\u003Cem>Women in the Storm\\u003C/em> is a feminist solo performance exploring the hidden barriers that can make escaping an abusive relationship so difficult.\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">Through a fictional woman's story shaped by real cases and testimonies, the performance traces her journey from love to control, from violence to resistance, and from seeking help to fighting for a way out. As she tries to leave, she finds herself caught between family expectations, social pressure, financial dependence, barriers to divorce, the struggle to prove abuse, and a legal system she desperately needs to protect her.\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">Blending monologue, physical theatre and documentary material, \\u003Cem>Women in the Storm\\u003C/em> asks us to look beyond the question, \\u003Cstrong>“when the storm comes, where is the way out?”\\u003C/strong> and instead confront what can stand in the way when someone tries to leave safely.\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">Because escaping violence should not mean gambling with your life.\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">\\u003Cem>The performance draws on documented cases and social realities. Its characters and central narrative are fictionalised for the stage.\\u003C/em>\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">\\u003Cstrong>Content Warning:\\u003C/strong> This performance contains depictions of domestic violence, emotional and physical abuse, and medical trauma, including references to injury, threats, and systemic injustice. Viewer discretion is advised.\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">\\u003Cstrong>A solo performance by Arina Yang.\\u003C/strong>\\u003C/span>\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#FACADE;--custom-color-dark:#FACADE\\\">\\u003Cstrong>Playwright &amp; Performer:\\u003C/strong>\\u003C/span>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\"> Arina (Yutong Yang)\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cstrong>Composer:\\u003C/strong> Ganey Ganyu Zhang\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cstrong>Voice Performer:\\u003C/strong> D’Jordelle Wright-Auguiste\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cstrong>Tech Operator:\\u003C/strong> Yi Cheng\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cstrong>Props &amp; Set Design:\\u003C/strong> Jade Jiayu Liu\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cstrong>Photographer:\\u003C/strong> Aaliyah Allotey\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cbr />\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">Instagram: @\\u003C/span>\\u003Ca rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" href=\\\"http://women.in\\\">\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">women.in\\u003C/span>\\u003C/a>\\u003Cspan style=\\\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#cdcdcd\\\">.the.storm\\u003C/span>\\u003C/p>\"}}],artists:[],seo:{jsonSchema:[{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",name:\"Women in the Storm\",url:\"https://events.humanitix.com/women-in-the-storm\",startDate:\"2026-10-18T19:00:00+0100\",endDate:\"2026-10-18T20:00:00+0100\",location:c,eventStatus:\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",eventAttendanceMode:\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",description:\"When the storm comes, where is the way out?\\n\\n\",image:\"https://images.humanitix.com/i/f46ba5a5-40b7-4677-879e-185ff8835832.jpeg@seo-500.jpg\",offers:d},{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",name:\"Women in the Storm\",url:\"