a-trap-boundary=\"last\" data-button-style=\"flat\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 15 15\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" class=\"CrossIcon\" aria-label=\"Cross icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Close icon</title><path d=\"M11.782 4.032a.575.575 0 1 0-.813-.814L7.5 6.687 4.032 3.218a.575.575 0 0 0-.814.814L6.687 7.5l-3.469 3.468a.575.575 0 0 0 .814.814L7.5 8.313l3.469 3.469a.575.575 0 0 0 .813-.814L8.313 7.5l3.469-3.468Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg><!----><span class=\"u-visually-hidden\">Close</span></button><!----><!----></dialog><!----></div><!----> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class=\"EventModules svelte-r64kdn\"><!--[--><!--[0--><!--[9--><div class=\"EventModuleRichText svelte-6ayzyh\"><!--[0--><h2 class=\"title f-heading-4 svelte-6ayzyh\">Description</h2><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <div class=\"RichContent f-body-3 svelte-jgfn07\"><!--[0--><!----><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">BRONSON is a powerful one-man theatrical exploration inspired by the extraordinary public persona and life surrounding one of Britain’s most notorious prisoners.</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Performed by Francis Saunders and directed by Sean Broughton, the production takes the audience inside a world of confinement, violence, humour, identity and survival.</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Moving between characters and states of mind, the performance explores the man behind the mythology and asks a much bigger question: when someone spends decades inside an institution, where does the individual end and the character created by that institution begin?</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Raw, physical and at times darkly funny, BRONSON is not presented as a factual biography. It is a piece of theatre inspired by themes of imprisonment, isolation, masculinity, institutionalisation and the human need to be seen.</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">CREATIVE TEAM</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">Performed by Francis Saunders<br />Directed by Sean Broughton<br />Assistant Director Dean Stalham<br />Producer Jo Morgan<br />Music De Crâne<br />Sound Jules Deering</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\">AGE RESTRICTION<br />16+</span></p><!----><!--]--></div><!----></div><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></div><!--]--> <div class=\"HumanitixBannerLarge svelte-17kav4o\"><div class=\"logos svelte-17kav4o\"><span class=\"powered-by f-label-1 svelte-17kav4o\">Powered by</span> <svg class=\"HumanitixLogoSvg svelte-pxa59x\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 139 34\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Humanitix logo</title><g><!--[-1--><!--]--><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M12.37 23.84c-1.06 0-1.62-.57-1.62-1.63v-2.73a.66.66 0 0 0-.72-.72H6.35a.66.66 0 0 0-.72.72v2.73c0 1.06-.56 1.63-1.62 1.63H1.62C.56 23.84 0 23.27 0 22.2v-10.2c0-1.06.56-1.62 1.62-1.62h2.4c1.05 0 1.61.56 1.61 1.62v1.84a.66.66 0 0 0 .72.72h3.68a.66.66 0 0 0 .72-.72v-1.84c0-1.06.56-1.62 1.62-1.62h2.4c1.05 0 1.61.56 1.61 1.62v10.2c0 1.06-.56 1.63-1.62 1.63h-2.4ZM19.05 20.53v-8.52c0-1.06.56-1.62 1.62-1.62h2.2c1.06 0 1.62.56 1.62 1.62v6.67c0 .92.67 1.02 1.18 1.02.52 0 1.03-.03 1.54-.1a.68.68 0 0 0 .66-.75V12c0-1.06.56-1.62 1.62-1.62h2.23c1.06 0 1.62.56 1.62 1.62v10.2c0 1.06-.56 1.63-1.62 1.63H30.5c-.78 0-1.28-.2-1.57-.64l-.06-.09a.64.64 0 0 0-.5-.3.68.68 0 0 0-.35.11 12.3 12.3 0 0 1-5.08 1.14c-2.59 0-3.9-1.19-3.9-3.53ZM53.74 23.84c-1.06 0-1.62-.57-1.62-1.63v-6.67c0-.7-.31-1-1.07-1h-.4c-.26 0-.5.03-.76.07a.74.74 0 0 0-.6.8v6.8c0 1.06-.56 1.63-1.63 1.63h-1.98c-1.06 0-1.62-.57-1.62-1.63v-6.67c0-.69-.34-1-1.1-1-.35 0-